  #line-at(90pt, 368.84pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 383.6pt, "A simple optical strategy to transform patchy PMMA–azopolymer composite nanoparticles into ")
  #line-at(90pt, 399.2pt, "complex, fully three-dimensional morphologies using controlled laser polarization is presented. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 414.8pt, "The particles consist of a PMMA core decorated with nanoscale azopolymer patches that undergo ")
  #line-at(90pt, 430.4pt, "localized photofluidization upon trans–cis isomerization. Linear polarization drives directed mass ")
  #line-at(90pt, 446pt, "transport within each patch, producing elongated super-cones that collectively yield porcupine-")
  #line-at(90pt, 461.6pt, "like particles, whereas circular polarization generates isotropic bump deformations reminiscent of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 477.2pt, "sea-pineapple structures. A nonlinear, volume-conserving geometric model quantitatively ")
  #line-at(90pt, 492.8pt, "reproduces the patch-to-filament transition. Brownian and Jeffery-flow simulations reveal that ")
  #line-at(90pt, 508.4pt, "these photoinduced morphologies dramatically alter hydrodynamic behavior, leading to enhanced ")
  #line-at(90pt, 524pt, "anisotropic diffusion, reduced rotational randomization, and polarization-dependent transport ")
  #line-at(90pt, 539.6pt, "amplification in shear flow. This light-driven, reversible sculpting method provides a versatile route ")
  #line-at(90pt, 555.2pt, "to programmable colloidal shapes and highlights geometry as a powerful control parameter for ")
  #line-at(90pt, 570.8pt, "microscale transport, active materials, and soft-matter physics. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.56pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 633.2pt, "Keywords")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(132.6pt, 633.2pt, ": ")
