#original-page(595pt, 842pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 99.56pt, "Introduction")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 114.8pt, "Polymeric particles have become remarkably important across a diverse range of fields, from ")
  #line-at(90pt, 130.4pt, "pharmaceuticals and advanced materials to personal care and medical imaging [1]. Their ")
  #line-at(90pt, 146pt, "interest lies in their adaptability, extending foundational research areas, such as microfluidics ")
  #line-at(90pt, 161.6pt, "and nanotechnology. A crucial point to highlight is the significant influence of particle shape ")
  #line-at(90pt, 177.2pt, "on functionality parameters such as microswimmer control, liquid flow dynamics, and motion ")
  #line-at(90pt, 192.8pt, "behavior [2]. These parameters show a highly shape-dependence on the viability of the results. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 208.4pt, "Historically, producing polymer particles with precise and varied shapes posed considerable ")
  #line-at(90pt, 224pt, "challenges, resulting in a predominance of simple, spherical forms. However, recent ")
  #line-at(90pt, 239.6pt, "technological advancements have led to new strategies for fabricating polymeric particles with ")
  #line-at(90pt, 255.2pt, "controlled, non-spherical geometries [3]. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 270.8pt, "Among polymer nanoparticles, polymeric Janus nanoparticles are colloidal objects whose ")
  #line-at(90pt, 286.4pt, "surfaces are deliberately divided into two (or more) chemically or physically distinct regions. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 302pt, "In the simplest case, each hemisphere is composed of a different polymer or carries ")
  #line-at(90pt, 317.6pt, "orthogonal functional groups, endowing the particle with an intrinsic directionality [4]. This ")
  #line-at(90pt, 333.2pt, "broken symmetry translates into emergent behaviors that are inaccessible to isotropic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 348.8pt, "spheres, positioning Janus nanoparticles at the intersection of advanced soft-matter physics ")
  #line-at(90pt, 364.4pt, "and programmable self-assembly. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 380pt, "Synthesis strategies have evolved rapidly over the past two decades. Seeded emulsion ")
  #line-at(90pt, 395.6pt, "polymerization and phase-segregating block-copolymer micellization were among the earliest ")
  #line-at(90pt, 411.2pt, "routes, but recent researches rely on microfluidic flow focusing [5], electrohydrodynamic co-")
  #line-at(90pt, 426.8pt, "jetting, and pickering-emulsion masking to tailor particle size (20 nm – 500 nm) and interfacial ")
  #line-at(90pt, 442.4pt, "sharpness [6, 7]. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 458pt, "The anisotropic architecture confers distinctive physicochemical characteristics. Under an ")
  #line-at(90pt, 473.6pt, "external field (electric, magnetic, or acoustic) Janus particles experience a net torque rather ")
  #line-at(90pt, 489.2pt, "than purely translational forces, enabling controlled orientation and propulsion like ")
  #line-at(90pt, 504.8pt, "microscopic ‘sailboats’ [8]. Interfacial tension gradients across the two faces give rise to self-")
  #line-at(90pt, 520.4pt, "propelling Marangoni flows, while selective functionalization allows orthogonal ")
  #line-at(90pt, 536pt, "bioconjugation—antibodies on one side, imaging dyes or drugs on the other—yielding ")
  #line-at(90pt, 551.6pt, "multifunctional nanocarriers that can navigate complex biological materials. Furthermore, the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 567.2pt, "directional dipole in surface energy facilitates hierarchical assembly into one-dimensional ")
  #line-at(90pt, 582.8pt, "chains, two-dimensional patchy crystals, or complex colloidal molecules, expanding the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 598.4pt, "toolbox for bottom-up materials fabrication. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 614pt, "Applications are correspondingly diverse. Photonic crystals derived from self-assembled Janus ")
  #line-at(90pt, 629.6pt, "colloids exhibit angle-independent structural coloration, promising eco-friendly pigments [9]. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 645.2pt, "Despite these advances, challenges remain and new shapes of polymer nanoparticles are still ")
  #line-at(90pt, 660.8pt, "in demand with active stimuli for changing the shape.  Azopolymer Janus nanoparticles merge ")
  #line-at(90pt, 676.4pt, "the light-responsive power of azobenzene chromophores with the directional functionality ")
  #line-at(90pt, 692pt, "characteristic of Janus architectures. Since the first reports demonstrating their fabrication ")
  #line-at(90pt, 707.6pt, "[10], research has progressed along different axes mainly synthetic methodology, photo-")
  #line-at(90pt, 723.2pt, "actuated mechanics.  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 738.8pt, "The important point of azopolymers is the reversible trans - cis photo-isomerization. Zhou et ")
  #line-at(90pt, 754.4pt, "al. reported ‘Azo-Polymer Janus Particles and Their Photoinduced Symmetry-Breaking ")
]

