#original-page(595pt, 842pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 83.6pt, "Deformation’ where methacrylate-based azopolymer (PAZO-ADMA) was combined with ")
  #line-at(90pt, 99.2pt, "PMMA to form micron-scale Janus particles. Under polarized light, only the azopolymer ")
  #line-at(90pt, 114.8pt, "hemisphere deforms, leading to controllable, reversible symmetry breaking and anisotropic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 130.4pt, "shape changes [11]. C. Liao et al. extended this concept to “Photodeformable Azo Polymer ")
  #line-at(90pt, 146pt, "Janus Particles obtained upon nonsolvent-induced phase separation and asynchronous ")
  #line-at(90pt, 161.6pt, "aggregation,” where phase separation during particle formation yields azopolymer-rich and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 177.2pt, "azopolymer-poor domains [12].  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 192.8pt, "In all these studies janus nanoparticles made with azopolymer have only two sides. Recently, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 208.4pt, "the possibility to have multiple side on the same sphere was demonstrated [13]. Preparation ")
  #line-at(90pt, 224pt, "of raspberry-like silica nanoparticles is fairly easy and well described in the literature [14]. The ")
  #line-at(90pt, 239.6pt, "possibility to fabricate high surface roughness like raspberry-like particles was demonstrated ")
  #line-at(90pt, 255.2pt, "[15]. C. Hsu et al. gave the first demonstration of Janus and strawberry particles using azo ")
  #line-at(90pt, 270.8pt, "molecular glass, photodeformable strawberry-like particles [16]. They presented a simple one-")
  #line-at(90pt, 286.4pt, "step fabrication method with microparticle’s morphology controlled by diffusion and solvent ")
  #line-at(90pt, 302pt, "quality effects. Strawberry-like particles (with EG) have partial phase separation leading to ")
  #line-at(90pt, 317.6pt, "small domains (patches). The Azo domains are distributed on PDMS matrix. The study aims to ")
  #line-at(90pt, 333.2pt, "fabricate and control complex microparticles (Janus and strawberry-like) made of: ")
  #line-at(90pt, 348.8pt, "- Azo molecular glass (IA-Chol) is photoresponsive, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 364.4pt, "- PDMS oligomer (H2pdca-PDMS) is flexible with low surface energy ")
  #line-at(90pt, 380pt, "and to understand the mechanism of their formation and behavior.  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 395.6pt, "The slow solvent evaporation in droplets creates phase separation between PDMS and azo ")
  #line-at(90pt, 411.2pt, "glass. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 426.8pt, "Adding Ethylene Glycol blocks gives a full segregation with switches morphology from Janus ")
  #line-at(90pt, 442.4pt, "to strawberry-like. The azo component enables light-controlled elongation and filaments only ")
  #line-at(90pt, 458pt, "on the supporting particle. However, the produced filaments are only on the basis of the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 473.6pt, "particle in contact with the substrate and not directly observed on the particle itself with ")
  #line-at(90pt, 489.2pt, "photoinduced patches.  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 504.8pt, "The new multi-janus azopolymer nanoparticles presented in this study can be photo-writable ")
  #line-at(90pt, 520.4pt, "on the different faces and due to the observed hairy surface is named porcupine nanoparticle. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 536pt, "Different morphologies could be accessible through a remote process. Finally, we show ")
  #line-at(90pt, 551.6pt, "through Brownian and Jeffery-flow simulations that these photoinduced geometries have ")
  #line-at(90pt, 567.2pt, "profound consequences for hydrodynamic behavior—including anisotropic diffusion, reduced ")
  #line-at(90pt, 582.8pt, "rotational randomization, and enhanced shear-induced dispersion—highlighting geometry as ")
  #line-at(90pt, 598.4pt, "a key regulator of microscale transport. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 629.6pt, "Materials and methods ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 645.2pt, "The synthesis of porcupine nanoparticles was done using a modified emulsion polymerization ")
  #line-at(90pt, 660.8pt, "technique to ensure the formation of a core-shell structure. The core consists of PMMA, while ")
  #line-at(90pt, 676.4pt, "the shell is made up of azopolymer fragments. The synthesis process is outlined as follows: ")
  #line-at(90pt, 692pt, "The porcupine nanoparticles were fabricated through a self-assembly approach by adding ")
  #line-at(90pt, 707.6pt, "water to a solution of the polymer in chloroform. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 723.2pt, "Polymers: 20 mg of azobenzene polymer and 20 mg of PMMA ((Aldrich, inherent viscosity ")
  #line-at(90pt, 738.8pt, "~1.25 dL/g) were dissolved in 2 ml of chloroform.  1 ml of the obtained solution was added ")
  #line-at(90pt, 754.4pt, "carefully into the bottom of aqueous solution of poly(vinyl alcohol (2,5 wt%, 30 ml) under ")
]

