#original-page(595pt, 842pt, (image("graphics/page-08.png", width: 414pt), 89.5pt, 273.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.923pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 84.8pt, "The time is normalized to the final time. The figure 4a present the evolution of the azopolymer ")
  #line-at(90pt, 102.68pt, "patch as a function of time starting from the semispherical shape to a filament or ‘super-cone’. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 120.68pt, "The volume is kept constant and the photoinduced phenomenon creates mass transport in a ")
  #line-at(90pt, 138.56pt, "single direction, that of the laser polarization. To produce the filament or super-cone, the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 156.56pt, "surface hollows out and the volume stretches upwards. Figure 4b shows the hollowing out of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 174.44pt, "the surface as a function of time. The radius of curvature of the surface is modeled as a ")
  #line-at(90pt, 192.44pt, "nonlinear function. The angle of curvature is plotted in Figure 4c as a function of time. The ")
  #line-at(90pt, 210.32pt, "evolution is almost linear. It is assumed that the change in shape of the cone is very rapid at ")
  #line-at(90pt, 228.32pt, "the beginning of illumination and slows down as the shape approaches that of the filament or ")
  #line-at(90pt, 246.2pt, "super-cone. In this case, the photoinduced phenomenon slows down and saturates because ")
  #line-at(90pt, 264.2pt, "there is less material to transport.     ")
  #line-at(90pt, 547.28pt, "Fig. 4: a) Simulation of evolution of the semi-spherical patch on the azopheres at different ")
  #line-at(90pt, 565.28pt, "times. The time is normalized to the final saturation of the photoinduced phenomenon, b) ")
  #line-at(90pt, 583.16pt, "variation of the patch‘s surface as a function of time, c) the angle of the cone is changed during ")
  #line-at(90pt, 601.16pt, "illumination.  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 637.04pt, "Following the further possibilities of surface deformations and new shapes using light, the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 654.92pt, "polarization of the laser was changed to circular polarization, with a quarter wave plate. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 672.92pt, "Initially patchy spherical particles containing the azopolymer patches on the surface were ")
  #line-at(90pt, 690.8pt, "illuminated by circular polarization for 15 minutes. The final structure of the particles is shown ")
  #line-at(90pt, 708.8pt, "in Figure 5. These particles resemble a sea pineapple. Under illumination with a circular ")
  #line-at(90pt, 726.68pt, "polarization, there is no any preferred direction of the movement for azopolymers. However, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 744.68pt, "through the ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.923pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(144.96pt, 744.68pt, "trans-cis")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.923pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(182.64pt, 744.68pt, " isomerization and movements of the azopolymers it was observed bump ")
  #line-at(90pt, 762.56pt, "shapes clearly visible on the particles resembling a seed or sea pineapple. ")
]

// arXiv source page 9
#original-page(595pt, 842pt, (image("graphics/page-09.png", width: 246.5pt), 173.5pt, 74pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(110.4pt, 364.04pt, "Fig. 5: Illumination of the new azopolymer microspheres with a circular polarization.  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 395.96pt, "Such similar particles were recently synthesized through a complicated three step process. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 413.84pt, "First, highly cross-linked seed particle dispersion was synthesized by emulsifier-free emulsion ")
  #line-at(90pt, 431.84pt, "polymerization with acrylic acid as co-monomer for the formation of surface carboxylic groups. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 449.72pt, "Then, a successive growth scheme was applied to the seeds by swelling the particles with ")
  #line-at(90pt, 467.72pt, "monomer droplets, followed by polymerization. The sea pineapple-shaped particles could be ")
  #line-at(90pt, 485.6pt, "produced by adjusting the amount of monomer during the swelling step of the third growth ")
  #line-at(90pt, 503.6pt, "[21]. Unlike the mentioned process, particles presented in the study using laser illumination ")
  #line-at(90pt, 521.48pt, "were obtained faster and with less effort after fabrication with the result of the mass transport ")
  #line-at(90pt, 539.48pt, "induced by the light as stimulus.  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 557.36pt, "As it was demonstrated in previous researches, inscription of gratings in the surface if ")
  #line-at(90pt, 575.36pt, "azopolymer thin films are done not only by an interference pattern of a double beam exp")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(481.68pt, 575.36pt, "osure ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 593.24pt, "[22], but also through a single beam experiment [23]. Following the method of SRG inscription, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 611.24pt, "a sample of these azopolymer particles were subjected to an interference pattern. The laser ")
  #line-at(90pt, 629.12pt, "beam was spatially filtered, collimated and then split by a beam splitter (BS) giving two beams ")
  #line-at(90pt, 647.12pt, "of equal intensity. The two beams, after reflecting from a mirror, are recombined to form an ")
  #line-at(90pt, 665pt, "interference pattern and were incident on the sample stage. As can be seen from Fig.6a-b, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 683pt, "upon exposure to the interference pattern a surface grating is inscribed on fragments of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 700.88pt, "azopolymer on the particles during the first 5 minutes of irradiation (Fig. 6a).  ")
]

// arXiv source page 10
#original-page(595pt, 842pt, (image("graphics/page-10.png", width: 416pt), 89.5pt, 76pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.923pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 209.6pt, "Fig. 6: laser illumination of porcupine nanoparticles with interference patterns. a) the fringes ")
  #line-at(90pt, 227.48pt, "are illuminating with a vertical polarization, b) with a horizontal polarization. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 259.76pt, "The pitch value (")
  #line-at(170.16pt, 259.76pt, ") for the gratings on these azo fragments (fig. 6a and b) is about 1.3 ± 0.1")
  #line-at(487.8pt, 259.76pt, "μ")
  #line-at(493.8pt, 259.76pt, "m, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 277.4pt, "which is in agreement with the degree of the interference pattern (")
  #line-at(399pt, 277.4pt, "θ")
  #line-at(404.76pt, 277.4pt, " = 10°). By continuous ")
  #line-at(90pt, 295.4pt, "illumination of the samples up to 10 minutes, the grating on the fragments become more ")
  #line-at(90pt, 313.28pt, "dominant and the movement and stretching of the azopolymer start. After 15 minutes of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 331.28pt, "irradiation, the particles are similar to the particles exposed to the single linearly polarized ")
  #line-at(90pt, 349.16pt, "beam, spiked like a porcupine (Fig. 6c). ")
  #line-at(90pt, 367.16pt, "One of the big advantages of azo incorporated polymers has been their reversibility. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 385.04pt, "Researchers working with these azobenzene based compounds in SRG formation and photo ")
  #line-at(90pt, 403.04pt, "deformation have been using methods such as circular polarization and unpolarized light to ")
  #line-at(90pt, 420.92pt, "reverse the effects applied to the surface and re-do the effects again. Given the fact that the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 438.92pt, "new particles consist in a layer of azopolymer patches, there should be a degree of reversibility ")
  #line-at(90pt, 456.8pt, "for the induced shapes on the particles. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 474.8pt, "In order to test this reversibility, one of the samples already subjected to linear polarization ")
  #line-at(90pt, 492.68pt, "(Fig. 7a) were irradiated by a beam of circular polarization for 15 minutes. Considering the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 510.68pt, "random directional movement of the azopolymers under such illumination, the spikes on the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 528.56pt, "porcupine particles retreat and change the porcupine shape particles into sea pineapple ")
  #line-at(90pt, 546.56pt, "particles (Fig. 7(b)). The super-cone undergoes photoisomerization, and the previously formed ")
  #line-at(90pt, 564.44pt, "filament flattens under the effect of light-induced mass transport.")
  #line-at(90pt, 748.52pt, "Fig. 7: a) initial particles with super-cone generated by the photoinduced process after ")
  #line-at(90pt, 766.4pt, "illumination with TE polarization, b) the same particle is illuminated with a circular polarization,  ")
]

// arXiv source page 11
#original-page(595pt, 842pt, (image("graphics/page-11.png", width: 362.5pt), 143pt, 363.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.923pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 84.8pt, "Considering the nature of the azopolymers and its photoinduced molecular mass transport, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 102.68pt, "new geometric changes of the particles through a directional polarization could be possible. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 120.68pt, "Hence, the same sample of patchy particles, now with pineapple-shape particles (Fig. 7b), was ")
  #line-at(90pt, 138.56pt, "again irradiated with a horizontally linear polarized laser beam. Once more, the formation of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 156.56pt, "‘porcupine’ particles as a result was observed (Fig. 7c).  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 174.44pt, "Beside the unique and exotic shape of these particles under laser illumination, stretching of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 192.44pt, "the azo fragments effect not only the shape of their particles, but also their coverage area. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 210.32pt, "Evaluations from the images show that, for a typical size buckyball particles (with a diameter ")
  #line-at(90pt, 228.32pt, "of 35")
  #line-at(113.4pt, 228.32pt, "μ")
  #line-at(119.4pt, 228.32pt, "m), azo fragments exposed to laser beam stretch about 13 ± 1")
  #line-at(400.8pt, 228.32pt, "μ")
  #line-at(406.8pt, 228.32pt, "m. This value is about ")
  #line-at(90pt, 246.2pt, "0.4 of the particles diameter, which leads to a particle that, now can cover an elliptical area ")
  #line-at(90pt, 264.2pt, "1.5 times more than the circular area it was covering before. The figure 8 shows the evolution ")
  #line-at(90pt, 282.08pt, "of the particle after irradiation (fig. 8d). Initially spherical (fig. 8a), the particle is elongated in ")
  #line-at(90pt, 300.08pt, "the direction of the laser polarization and stretch. The stretching is not comparable to a pure ")
  #line-at(90pt, 317.96pt, "azopolymer particle. However, the ellipticity is increased by a factor 0.2 (fig. 8b). A model ")
  #line-at(90pt, 335.96pt, "calculating the elongation of the particle is done and shows the results of the ellipticity after ")
  #line-at(90pt, 353.84pt, "irradiation (fig. 8c, SI4). ")
  #line-at(90pt, 715.04pt, "Fig. 8: a) initial particle before irradiation, b) final shape of the particle after illumination, c) ")
  #line-at(90pt, 732.92pt, "evolution of the curvature radius. The photoinduced phenomenon not only shapes the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 750.92pt, "patches in super-cone but stretches the particles itself. The time is normalized to the final. ")
]

// arXiv source page 12
#original-page(595pt, 842pt, (image("graphics/page-12.png", width: 83pt), 262.5pt, 413.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 84.8pt, "Availability of polymeric particles with distinct shapes will prove to be a useful tool in ")
  #line-at(90pt, 102.68pt, "uncovering the role of shape in applications such as biological systems. Particles can be used ")
  #line-at(90pt, 120.68pt, "as models for similar- looking objects, like bacteria or pollen grain, not only in biological ")
  #line-at(90pt, 138.56pt, "applications but also in environmental fields to study bacterial migration in soil or water. In ")
  #line-at(90pt, 156.56pt, "another field, non-spherical particles also may open new applications in advanced materials ")
  #line-at(90pt, 174.44pt, "due to their unique scattering and packing properties. These particles also can be used as ")
  #line-at(90pt, 192.44pt, "research tools or probes in rheology or aerodynamics or as sensors in micro-rheology studies. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 210.32pt, "The uses and knowledge gained from particles with defined shapes seem limitless, and the ")
