  #line-at(248.16pt, 233.36pt, "/2). This anisotropy has several dynamical consequences. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 248.96pt, "First, the instantaneous Brownian steps become elongated, generating trajectories that show ")
  #line-at(90pt, 264.56pt, "short-time directionality even in the absence of external forces or flows. Second, because ")
  #line-at(90pt, 280.16pt, "rotational diffusion is simultaneously reduced (owing to the larger rotational radius R")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(473.04pt, 281.12pt, "rot")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(481.32pt, 280.16pt, "), the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 295.76pt, "orientation vector p(t) decorrelates more slowly, allowing the particle to maintain its direction ")
  #line-at(90pt, 311.36pt, "of fastest diffusion for extended periods. The joint effect is a transient regime of superficially ")
  #line-at(90pt, 326.96pt, "persistent or ‘quasi-ballistic’ Brownian motion, visible in the MSD as an early-time slope higher ")
  #line-at(90pt, 342.56pt, "than that of an equivalent smooth sphere (fig. SI7). At longer times, full rotational ")
  #line-at(90pt, 358.16pt, "randomization restores isotropy in the ensemble average, but with a larger effective diffusivity ")
  #line-at(90pt, 373.76pt, "than the spherical particle because the particle spends more time moving along directions ")
  #line-at(90pt, 389.36pt, "where diffusion is intrinsically faster. This behavior is characteristic of anisotropic colloids such ")
  #line-at(90pt, 404.96pt, "as rods, ellipsoids, and biologically inspired particles [26], and here it emerges purely from the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 420.56pt, "hierarchical spiky geometry of the porcupine particle. Importantly, the model isolates ")
  #line-at(90pt, 436.16pt, "morphology as the sole source of anisotropy: no chemical activity, flow alignment, or ")
  #line-at(90pt, 451.76pt, "hydrodynamic torques are present. Thus, the observed enhancement and transient ")
  #line-at(90pt, 467.36pt, "directionality in the MSD provide a clear quantitative signature of how geometry alone—and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 482.96pt, "specifically the condition D")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(209.88pt, 483.92pt, "∥")
