  #line-at(90pt, 426.8pt, "Conclusion ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 442.4pt, "In this work, a straightforward optical method to fabricate complex azopolymer–PMMA ")
  #line-at(90pt, 458pt, "composite nanoparticles whose shapes can be reversibly sculpted with light is presented. The ")
  #line-at(90pt, 473.6pt, "patchy azopolymer surface enables localized, polarization-controlled photo-fluidization, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 489.2pt, "allowing spherical particles to transform into filaments, spikes, or isotropic bumps. This ")
  #line-at(90pt, 504.8pt, "bottom-up strategy offers access to shapes called porcupine and sea-pineapple ")
  #line-at(90pt, 520.4pt, "morphologies—that are difficult or impossible to obtain using conventional multi-step ")
  #line-at(90pt, 536pt, "synthetic routes. A nonlinear geometric model accurately reproduces the experimentally ")
  #line-at(90pt, 551.6pt, "observed patch-to-cone transformation and captures the rapid–then-saturating dynamics of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 567.2pt, "photoinduced mass transport. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 582.8pt, "Beyond shape control, we show that these optical deformations drastically modify the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 598.4pt, "particles’ hydrodynamic behavior. The porcupine geometry generates strong anisotropic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 614pt, "Brownian diffusion, slow rotational decorrelation, and Jeffery-orbit-enhanced dispersion in ")
  #line-at(90pt, 629.6pt, "shear flow. Even modest geometric modifications, such as photoinduced super-cones at the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 645.2pt, "poles of an ellipsoid, significantly alter orientation statistics and translational transport. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 660.8pt, "Together, these findings reveal geometry as a powerful and tunable element of colloidal ")
  #line-at(90pt, 676.4pt, "design. The ease of fabrication, reversibility, and dynamical consequences of these new ")
  #line-at(90pt, 692pt, "particles open promising perspectives for responsive materials, optical micromanipulation, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 707.6pt, "biological model systems, and next-generation micro- and nanoscale transport studies. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(487.68pt, 707.6pt, "One ")
  #line-at(90pt, 723.08pt, "possible method to ensure an efficient homogeneous illumination is to do the illumination in a ")
  #line-at(90pt, 738.68pt, "microfluidic channel with a periodic sorting of micro-particles and a control of the flow.")
