  #line-at(90pt, 270.8pt, "surface curvature and patch multiplicity as platforms for multivalent biochemical interactions. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 286.4pt, "In this perspective, the porcupine morphology is not only a physical curiosity but a ")
  #line-at(90pt, 302pt, "programmable scaffold that merges optical actuation, directional transport control, and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 317.6pt, "biofunctional surface engineering—opening avenues toward light-driven theranostic micro-")
  #line-at(90pt, 333.2pt, "objects, active diagnostic probes, and adaptive nanomedicine systems.  ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 348.8pt, "For transverse")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(157.44pt, 348.8pt, " applications—particularly in microfluidics, biosensing, or biomedical ")
  #line-at(90pt, 364.4pt, "environments—the particle size and long-term structural stability must be carefully ")
  #line-at(90pt, 380pt, "considered. The current micrometric dimensions (~40 µm) are well suited for deterministic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 395.6pt, "manipulation in laminar microflows, optical trapping, and shear-controlled transport, while ")
  #line-at(90pt, 411.2pt, "avoiding rapid Brownian randomization. However, for in vivo or capillary-scale applications, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 426.8pt, "size downscaling strategies (e.g., emulsification parameter optimization or microfluidic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 442.4pt, "synthesis) could be implemented to access the sub-10 µm regime while preserving patch ")
